From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Rau <alex@retroduction.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: edma: spread Rx ring interrupts over the cores

The EDMA driver maps the PPE queues of each core to its own Rx
descriptor ring (one ring per core) and distributes received flows over
those queues by hash, expecting the ring interrupts to be assigned to
different cores. Nothing assigns them, so all Rx rings are serviced on
the boot CPU and receive throughput is limited by a single core.

Set the affinity (and hint) of each Rx ring interrupt to its core when
the interrupts are requested, and clear the hint before they are freed.
User space (irqbalance, /proc/irq) can still override it.

On an IPQ9574 board (UniFi Cloud Gateway Fiber) a 16-stream TCP receive
test over a 10G link went from 3.86 to 6.45 Gbit/s with this change
(1.94 to 5.10 Gbit/s on a kernel without the board's MX rail vote).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Alex Rau <alex@retroduction.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma.c
@@ -436,6 +436,13 @@ static int edma_irq_register(void)
 			goto rx_desc_ring_intr_req_fail;
 		}
 
+		/* Each Rx desc ring serves the PPE queues of one core (see
+		 * edma_cfg_rx_rps_hash_map()), so steer its interrupt to that
+		 * core instead of leaving all rings on the boot CPU.
+		 */
+		irq_set_affinity_and_hint(edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i],
+					  cpumask_of(i % num_possible_cpus()));
+
 		pr_debug("RXDESC ring: %d IRQ:%d request success: %s\n",
 			 rx->ring_start + i,
 			 edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i],
@@ -458,6 +465,7 @@ misc_intr_req_fail:
 	/* Free IRQ for RXDESC rings */
 	for (i = 0; i < rx->num_rings; i++) {
 		synchronize_irq(edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i]);
+		irq_update_affinity_hint(edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i], NULL);
 		free_irq(edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i],
 			 (void *)&edma_ctx->rx_rings[i]);
 	}
@@ -799,6 +807,7 @@ void edma_destroy(struct ppe_device *ppe
 	/* Free IRQ for Rx DESC rings */
 	for (i = 0; i < rx->num_rings; i++) {
 		synchronize_irq(edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i]);
+		irq_update_affinity_hint(edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i], NULL);
 		free_irq(edma_ctx->intr_info.intr_rx[i],
 			 (void *)&edma_ctx->rx_rings[i]);
 		kfree(edma_rxdesc_irq_name[i]);
